{
  "description": "host-ops fixtures. scripts/verify.mjs runs each case against a copy of the shipped part outside the repository. Sources are relative to this folder, or to the part folder when they start with assets/. scan-host and check-plist cases read text and run anywhere (check-plist adds plutil -lint on macOS). probe-launchd cases judge a recorded launchctl print output against a copy of plist in a scratch folder; @DIR@ in a recording stands for that folder, and exit is the recorded run's exit code. A fail case must exit 1 with an error for its rule; a pass case must report its rule as passed with no error for it; a warn case must warn.",
  "cases": [
    { "id": "scan-shipped-assets", "rule": ["HO-ENV-01", "HO-PIPE-01", "HO-PRIV-01", "HO-TMP-01"], "expect": "pass", "checker": "scan-host", "sources": ["assets/env-value.sh", "assets/com.example.sync.plist"] },
